+### [Tile Range Identification](5135-tile-range-identification.md)
+Determines the contiguous start and end indices of each tile's Gaussian splats within a globally sorted list of projected 2D Gaussian keys. It sets itself apart from culling methods by operating on the post-sort data structure to define access bounds rather than filtering splats, and from [Tile-based Rasteriser](2846-tile-based-rasteriser.md) by preceding the actual pixel compositing phase. Choose it to map the flat, sorted array back to per-tile ranges for efficient iteration.
 
 ### [FlashGS](7331-flashgs.md)
